{
  "schema": "fcpi.budget-policy/v1",
  "comment": "Provider spending (FIRECRAWL_PI_SPEC.md §10, §14, §15, §28.3; PI_BUDGET_POLICY_FILE). The residential proxy has the owner's approved cap of 1000000 micro-USD a day and 2000000 a month (2026-10-15), kept low so its use can be measured: the residential route answers a block of the home connection, never volume. LLM extraction has an approved $20 monthly cap (2026-10-15), with no LLM-specific daily cap and, since 2026-10-17, no shared daily cap across the paid categories (the Anthropic credits are promotional); each paid category keeps its own caps. A shared daily cap set later counts only the reservations made while it is set. Parser and enhanced retrieval caps remain zero; PI_PAID_DISPATCH_ENABLED must also be true before a paid provider is called. Amounts are integers: micro-USD (1e-6 USD) or parser credits. A model or parser the policy does not list is refused; one without a rate card in effect is refused (fail closed). Fixture providers are unpaid and draw on their own categories, so the accounting runs end to end without money.",
  "notifyAtFraction": 0.8,
